      </div>
      <div style="position:absolute;bottom:-18px;right:-14px;background:#2E6B47;color:#fff;border-radius:20px;padding:14px 22px;box-shadow:0 10px 26px rgba(47,163,77,0.4);">
        <p style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;margin:0;line-height:1;">Spring</p>
        <p style="font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;margin:4px 0 0;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;">Storm Season</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="kicker">Fencing Dallas homeowners ask about</span>
      <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,40px);margin:0 0 18px;">Fencing in Dallas, with the city rules and the price ranges in plain view</h2>
      <div class="rich"><p>White Rock Fence Co is a Dallas-based advertising site for independent fence contractors. It does not build, repair or install anything itself, and it does not hold a contractor registration. What it does is put the facts a Dallas homeowner needs in one place: advertised price ranges with the firm named, what the City of Dallas says about permits and heights, and how the suburbs differ.</p><p>If you are deciding between patching and replacing, start with <a href="/fence-repair-dallas/">fence repair in Dallas</a> and the <a href="/fence-cost-dallas/">Dallas fence cost guide</a>. If it is a new 6-foot or 8-foot privacy fence, read <a href="/fence-installation-dallas/">fence installation in Dallas</a> first. Then call <strong>(214) 555-0137</strong> and ask for written quotes.</p></div>
      <a href="/about/" class="btn-blue" style="margin-top:10px;">More About Us</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .intro-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; gap: 44px !important; } }
</style>

