<!-- SERVICE CARDS -->
<section style="padding:0 24px 80px;background:#F6F3EE;">
  <div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <div class="svc-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <a href="/fence-installation-dallas/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">Wood & Privacy Fence Installation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">Replacing a worn 6-foot fence or stepping up to board-on-board with cedar pickets and steel posts. One DFW firm advertises installed cedar privacy fence at $18 to $28 per linear foot, while another advertises $30 to $60 for a 6-foot wood fence, so prices vary widely.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2E6B47;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/fence-repair-dallas/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">Fence Repair</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">Leaning posts, missing pickets and storm-damaged sections. One Dallas firm advertises a single post reset with new concrete at $150 to $400 and board replacement at $25 to $60 per board.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2E6B47;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/gate-repair-dallas/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">Gate Repair & Automatic Gates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">Sagging walk gates, worn hinges, dead openers and sliding tracks. Power wiring for an opener is electrical work, so ask the installer who holds the electrical license.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2E6B47;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/iron-fence-dallas/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">Wrought Iron & Ornamental Fences</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">Iron or steel pickets for a front yard or a side-yard run. One Dallas-area firm advertises residential tubular steel fence at $30 to $45 per linear foot installed.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2E6B47;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
