<!-- PROCESS -->
<section style="padding:76px 24px;background:#F6F3EE;">
  <div style="max-width:1020px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">
    <span class="kicker">How It Works</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,38px);margin:0 0 44px;">Three Steps: Describe, Quote, Build.</h2>
    <div class="steps-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:32px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:16px;padding:34px 26px;box-shadow:0 4px 18px rgba(10,61,92,0.08);">
        <div style="width:54px;height:54px;border-radius:50%;background:#2E6B47;color:#fff;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:800;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin:0 auto 16px;">1</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">Call or email and describe the fence</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5B5F62;margin:0;">Tell us what you have: a leaning wood fence, a storm gap, a dead gate opener or a new 8-foot board-on-board run. Mention your HOA and whether a dog is loose in the yard.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:16px;padding:34px 26px;box-shadow:0 4px 18px rgba(10,61,92,0.08);">
        <div style="width:54px;height:54px;border-radius:50%;background:#2E6B47;color:#fff;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:800;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin:0 auto 16px;">2</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">An independent contractor scopes the job</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5B5F62;margin:0;">The contractor will want the linear feet, the height, the material and any gates, and may look at the site, including alley access and corner-lot sight lines. Texas811 says that when you hire a contractor, calling 811 before digging is the contractor's job.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:16px;padding:34px 26px;box-shadow:0 4px 18px rgba(10,61,92,0.08);">
        <div style="width:54px;height:54px;border-radius:50%;background:#2E6B47;color:#fff;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:800;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin:0 auto 16px;">3</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">Compare written quotes</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5B5F62;margin:0;">You get a written quote from the contractor. Get two or three, check that each lists the same height, posts, pickets and gate hardware, and ask each about city registration and proof of insurance.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
